# Optional: use your own TURN relay instead of the free public one.
#
# You do not need any of this. Out of the box the app falls back to Metered's
# Open Relay, which is free, needs no account, and allows 20GB of relayed
# traffic a month shared across everyone using it.
#
# Set your own only if you would rather not share that quota - a free account at
# metered.ca gives you credentials, and Cloudflare and Twilio both offer relays
# too. ALL THREE values are required; a partial set is ignored on purpose,
# because a relay with the wrong credentials does not fail loudly, it just
# quietly never connects.
#
# These are compiled into the JavaScript that ships to the browser, so treat
# them as public. That is unavoidable for a browser app with no backend to mint
# short-lived credentials, and it is why the default is a relay whose
# credentials are published anyway. Never put anything genuinely secret here.
#
# On Vercel: Project Settings -> Environment Variables, then redeploy.

# VITE_TURN_URLS=turn:your.relay:3478,turns:your.relay:5349
# VITE_TURN_USERNAME=your-username
# VITE_TURN_CREDENTIAL=your-credential


# Optional: the mailbox, so the two of you do not have to be online at once.
#
# Without this the app syncs phone-to-phone, which needs both phones awake and
# both apps open at the same moment. With it, whatever either of you writes is
# waiting for the other next time they open the app. Deploy instructions and the
# reasoning are in worker/README.md.
#
# BOTH values are required. A URL with no token gets a 401 on every call, which
# would read as "sync is broken" rather than "sync is not set up", so a partial
# set is ignored on purpose - same rule as the TURN credentials above.
#
# The token is compiled into the JavaScript that ships to the browser, so it is
# public. It stops a passer-by burning your request quota; it is not a password
# and must not be one you use anywhere else. What actually keeps the mailbox
# private is its address, which is derived from your passphrase and which the
# Worker will not enumerate.
#
# If you point VITE_MAILBOX_URL at a custom domain rather than workers.dev, add
# that origin to connect-src in vercel.json and index.html or the browser will
# block it - and a CSP block looks exactly like "the mailbox did not help".

# VITE_MAILBOX_URL=https://our-space-mailbox.your-subdomain.workers.dev
# VITE_MAILBOX_TOKEN=a-long-random-string
